- All sabotage restores byte-identical; final baseline FAIL exit 1.
Evidence: cycle2-f3-negative-probe.log

R1 (residual finding, reported, NOT fixed): the denial filter is a regex
allowlist (`^(none|no|not|never|nothing)\b|not\s+obtainable|unobtainable|could\s+not\s+be`).
Paraphrased denials are accepted as observations; proven with a scratch q03:
  "Negative case: couldn't be reproduced"     -> accepted (failure came only from the count)
  "Negative case: unable to reproduce it"     -> accepted
  "Negative case: does not reproduce"         -> accepted
Impact: once a shape-deciding question is answered, a denial phrased outside
the allowlist satisfies the marker requirement. Currently masked by the four
NOT PERFORMED rows, so it flips nothing today; it is a real gap in the fix as
stated. Suggested direction (not applied): invert to require a positive
observation shape (command/exit/observed markers) instead of enumerating denials.

